    "created_at": "2019-09-09T11:43:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-09T11:46:07Z",
    "body": "Right, that makes total sense. There are several ways to get a high-resolution time on macOS, including through Python, Perl, and GNU date if the Homebrew coreutils formula is installed (available as `gdate`).\r\n\r\nFor example, if someone wants to implement this, here's a drop-in replacement for `date '+%s%0N'`:\r\n\r\n```\r\npython -c 'import time; print(int(time.time()*1e6))'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis might require some runtime detection, either for python (either 2 or 3) or to use this fallback only on macOS (which ships with Python).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
