    "body": "@chipbuster If curious, I still have the `time` runs on my terminal:\r\n```zsh\r\n➜ time python -c 'import time; print(int(time.time()*1e6))'\r\n1568041323133593\r\npython -c 'import time; print(int(time.time()*1e6))'  0.03s user 0.01s system 36% cpu 0.098 total\r\n\r\n➜ time date '+%s%0N'\r\n1568041329534595985\r\ndate '+%s%0N'  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.003 total\r\n```\r\nEven a python no-op is still much slower:\r\n```zsh\r\n➜ time python -c ''\r\npython -c ''  0.02s user 0.01s system 33% cpu 0.096 total\r\n```\r\nI know the times aren't too high, but with all the little slowdowns of different modules in starship, those add up to a lot of noticeable and irritating times.\r\n\r\nAnd also `python` is python2 here, python3 starts even slower than python2 here.",
